It may seem strange that you park in the handicap parking spots despite not having a disability, but there may be a few reasons why. Many states and local governments issue citations to those who wrongly use disabled-person placard or plates if it is obvious they don't qualify, and others issue fines for those without the special placard who use the disabled space without a permit or placard. Another reason is to show your support; those with limited mobility rely on these special spaces more frequently so they have easier access when entering and exiting public places. Finally, those without the need to use those spaces should try to refrain from doing it and leave more of them available for those who do need them.
